---
title: Lemon Drizzle Cake
author: Mary Berry
servings: 8
prep time: 20 min
cook time: 45 min
---

Preheat the oven to 180°C, gas mark 4. Grease and line a #900g loaf tin{} with baking parchment. In a bowl, use electric beaters to cream together @butter{100%g}(softened) and @golden caster sugar{150%g} for ~{3-4%minutes} until fluffy and very pale. Beat in @eggs{2}(lightly beaten), then sift in @self-raising flour{150%g} and mix well to combine. Stir in @whole milk{3%tbsp} and the zest of @lemons{2}.

Spoon the mixture into the prepared loaf tin and bake for about ~{45%minutes} until a skewer inserted into the centre of the cake comes out clean.

Ten minutes before the cake is cooked through, heat the juice of @lemons{2} and @granulated sugar{50%g} in a pan until the sugar has dissolved; set aside.

Remove the cake from the oven and, while still hot and in its tin, prick the surface all over with a skewer. Drizzle over the hot lemon syrup, then leave the cake to cool completely in the tin before cutting into thick slices to serve. Garnish with extra lemon zest, if liked.
